WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.720
Weak encryption reduces the protection expected for sensitive information.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:09.380
Applications should avoid outdated algorithms, custom cryptography, hard-coded secrets,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.040
weak randomness, and poor password hashing practices.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.140
Missing TLS or poor certificate validation can expose credentials, session tokens,

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.560
API traffic, and sensitive records in transit.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:27.620
Secure transport must be applied consistently across browsers, APIs, internal services,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.200
and integrations. Improper key handling can undermine otherwise strong cryptography.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:39.020
Keys need protected storage, controlled access, rotation, separation from protected data,

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.000
and lifecycle management.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:47.300
Sensitive data exposure also happens through logs, backups, debug output, caches, exports,

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.000
and unnecessary application responses.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.300
Teams should minimize sensitive data collection and control where it appears.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.240
Use strong encryption and vetted libraries.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:01.380
Validate certificates and enforce secure TLS configuration.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.360
Manage keys through protected, access-controlled processes.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:14.140
Selected CMMC mappings for this topic include SC.L2-3.13.8 - Confidentiality in transit;

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:19.720
SC.L2-3.13.11 - Cryptographic protections.
